  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing the Urgent Needs of Vulnerable Myanmar Nationals and Other Vulnerable Populations Affected by the Myanmar Crisis in Thailand</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The multi-dimensional crisis in Myanmar is gravely exacerbating human insecurity in the country, leading to amplified mobility of the affected population. In addition to the humanitarian crisis and human security elements driving migration from Myanmar, regional issues such as the recent trend of human trafficking for the purposes of forced criminality and increasing mobility of Rohingya refugees in the region are contributing to the complexity of human mobility. 
 
In response, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) in Thailand aims to enhance access to humanitarian assistance and build resilience of Myanmar nationals and other vulnerable groups in Thailand that are affected by the situation in Myanmar. This is being carried out through a two-pronged approach: securing access for Myanmar nationals and other vulnerable groups to humanitarian and specialized protection assistance and basic services to meet their immediate needs; and enhancing the resilience of Myanmar nationals through access to decent work and community-led services.</narrative>
  </description>
